 trusted deadline, continue observing; at or after the deadline, contact the receiver operator to investigate. An overdue `QUEUED` state does not by itself prove business failure or event loss.\n\nHTTP 202 alone proves acceptance only; without current same-event receiver evidence, the processing state is `UNKNOWN`. Do not infer the target event's state from elapsed time, a different event, an order snapshot, or historical advice. Never resend automatically.\n", "contract_versions": [2], "digest": "5fb3732339600ad1332960df08a00299358b8c4ea47c20f6fedc39b568c9850e", "document_id": "receiver-ack-contract-v2", "expires_at": "2030-01-01T00:00:00+00:00", "file": "receiver-ack-contract-v2-1.md", "keywords": ["202", "receiver", "queue", "accepted", "processed", "processing_sla_seconds", "����", "�Ŷ�", "SLA"], "source": "local:orders-async-demo/contract-v2.1", "title": "Receiver acknowledgement and processing SLA v2", "valid_from": "2026-10-25T00:00:00+00:00", "version": "2.1.0"}], "selected_skill_method_only": null, "skill_catalog": [{"description": "Use when order lifecycle is not yet established or HTTP 200 may be confused with completion; verify order first.", "name": "order-lifecycle-triage"}, {"description": "Use after a completed order: correlate delivery event, retry/failure details, acknowledgement and receiver queue; never resend.", "name": "callback-delivery-triage"}], "trusted_binding": {"contract_version": 2, "route": "/api/async-orders/async-order", "service_id": "orders-async-demo", "task_id": "task-4f70b968-8dfb-42ac-84f6-9e9b05d2987f"}, "unexecuted_candidates": [], "untrusted_user_inputs": [{"accepted_control_revision": 0, "applied_control_revision": 0, "body": "���� 200 ���ص���δ��ɣ���˶ԡ�", "digest": "26026039ab9fc8a5821f37fe9d659d742a27a60e97c3b9388b5c12eba39baa81", "input_kind": "CHAT_READONLY", "kind": "INITIAL_SYMPTOM", "message_id": "message-fce20162-9ae7-4ce9-9b7a-9d6dc00e60b1", "provenance": "USER_INPUT_UNTRUSTED", "sequence": 1}, {"accepted_control_re